{"id": "clm:0a7e08e2d66860472b6b13e06b6595dbccdf864ce12349e64ee451675313a466", "type": "statement", "text": "When reviewing a collection in Compass, unnecessary indexes and bloated documents are legitimate investigation targets. MongoDB documents their disk-space, write-cost, and query-performance consequences; the presence of an index or a large document alone does not establish that it is unnecessary or bloated. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/design-antipatterns.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4af3cc6c313505a90056944d20166ca893441e2dbd7a00c10de1fb872865ccdf"]}
{"id": "clm:d3bbde106c94a773c2cc2572c73a60ef08760ac669a7e250e7685bf412328516", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB's schema anti-pattern catalogue covers unbounded arrays, excessive collection counts, unnecessary indexes, bloated documents, and excessive $lookup operations. Independent research catalogues related MongoDB smells; its literature synthesis is corroborating context, not an independent measurement of Compass detection coverage. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/design-antipatterns.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://susi.usi.ch/documents/329705/files/Nagy_Lanza_2024_IEEE_SANER.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4af3cc6c313505a90056944d20166ca893441e2dbd7a00c10de1fb872865ccdf", "ev:983cf1c2435cd9b88a0f5a91a9b9e0d6b3cae9baf3518d5a4ec8abf64174eb3c", "ev:c29a051164b8c418c19cfe9b20f006fe98ecb4ae245bf16e894166a185edc6fe"]}
{"id": "clm:84d1b1946467d2350df965fa6124076e94c225f358b1fe679dc9d111a86407c4", "type": "statement", "text": "Allowing an embedded array to grow without a bound can exhaust document-size limits and impose resource costs. MongoDB documents its 16 MB BSON limit; independent document-database research reports the same general growth hazard. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/design-antipatterns/unbounded-arrays.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol18/p4804-carey.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:48c323f4e6b49bf5ef3159e2de0eb3e51f6b00cb23607e37c6275054ea6a8e81", "ev:69f66c962b983c55c72847dd99189c058079a68c105babd78ee75c609080e94c"]}
{"id": "clm:5ff8d7f3e4a973cccdb848fe65589da958afd5fc85a91cf4abbb86b616694ec0", "type": "statement", "text": "An anti-pattern warning does not justify banning arrays. MongoDB recommends bounded subsets for some access patterns, while independent research treats a bounded order-line array as sensible and an entire customer order history as unsafe nesting. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/design-antipatterns/unbounded-arrays.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol18/p4804-carey.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3dfafea9683c9887dca69acc4133ff271b4e5cf56d38199fae61518960c19165", "ev:69f66c962b983c55c72847dd99189c058079a68c105babd78ee75c609080e94c"]}
{"id": "clm:de8ce3ff0ea2f5b4237b9c8871e1166491953ed9394df8de29ce56498a50c27f", "type": "statement", "text": "COMPASS-9163 reports that importing a numeric embedding array of 251 elements triggers a large-array warning. Its report distinguishes import warning logic from schema insight logic. This establishes a reported warning mismatch, not universal behavior across Compass releases. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-06-19)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/COMPASS-9163", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:924c02e37352bbc099dac495c157e9fe629db370720282042d74d659a5fb7e57", "ev:ca323d6046bff356ee27c47ce723594bf9cb17148836d7c42e6a81a1368a56e9"]}
{"id": "clm:7765c4e83963149d674ff6dc994f1fd3b0436a6d2d5844ce5b6a7a11a7005509", "type": "statement", "text": "Treating a Compass schema sample as a complete data-quality audit is an anti-pattern. Sampling can omit rare fields or type variants; use targeted checks for exceptional records before concluding that they do not exist. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/compass/sampling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-compass-schema-analysis/view"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:89328a4226bb751c9023c439c3cb5e6fff680d493be2c108ad8218c4e688b114", "ev:e5b0820416bf1a9b86e1df0047ca695db12fa0a4e420c7b1c018b52de7ea93eb"]}
{"id": "clm:6c5cbe11526f7085ca5d58029160084f311b720c21ae9182d0b43b7b719fda65", "type": "statement", "text": "An embedded history that grows without a bound is a design risk even when it initially looks convenient in Compass. Growing arrays can strain resources and eventually exceed document limits; bounded subsets or separately stored related records can address the growth. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/design-antipatterns/unbounded-arrays.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol18/p4804-carey.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bac53774a3b9bb170989faef8a31105206755b444737e3b78596b54ad63289c9"]}
{"id": "clm:cdb6e382f0b01f69d8a3f308342777d2b49e405032f4619c99c00363d175992c", "type": "statement", "text": "Fixing unbounded arrays involves trade-offs: a bounded subset duplicates data and makes updates more expensive, while external references can require additional queries and latency. Select the remedy for the workload rather than treating every join as a design error. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/design-antipatterns/unbounded-arrays.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol18/p4804-carey.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2b54c5a4932c860c395e42525fc9f398326cc4cd5b9dfa0d98b5c5ca5c96e1d9"]}
{"id": "clm:b7e1d45e01000d75587122b264c55d9374f47dd8c81183a71bfce344a88b3fe8", "type": "statement", "text": "Increasing schema-analysis coverage has a cost: larger samples or whole-collection inspection require more time and processing. Use query filters to investigate relevant document segments rather than assuming one broad sample answers every question. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/compass/sampling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-compass-schema-analysis/view"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:38403a00f2415685a54d3932381ffee8be012faf9f51928a27cc713d3040e9c6", "ev:e5b0820416bf1a9b86e1df0047ca695db12fa0a4e420c7b1c018b52de7ea93eb"]}
{"id": "clm:fcaa5719b0877d233e81bd021d2914c6e6ab85d10b4b6fdff4255bb8964370ca", "type": "statement", "text": "Replacing embedded objects with an ever-growing array of their IDs does not necessarily remove unbounded growth. The document-database design paper explicitly warns about customer documents that retain every order reference; assess the cardinality and growth of references as well as embedded objects. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol18/p4804-carey.pdf", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/design-antipatterns/unbounded-arrays.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:69f66c962b983c55c72847dd99189c058079a68c105babd78ee75c609080e94c"]}
{"id": "clm:f0bd94d892b506fdda6c16f5ff79558f1033015d290f15ddf8bb06ff4110d5ca", "type": "statement", "text": "Unnecessary indexes and bloated documents deserve explicit review: the vendor describes storage and write costs from excess indexes and common-query costs from large documents; the research mapping reports the same categories and working-set pressure. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/design-antipatterns.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://susi.usi.ch/documents/329705/files/Nagy_Lanza_2024_IEEE_SANER.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0114843e4647c1c39bc3b04d7eebd9e9295f7e0380fc4ed73f120eecd205e5e9", "ev:1d4676077e3faca79270a3a99a954614848f724eb59265a6436ee058c42d0dd1", "ev:4af3cc6c313505a90056944d20166ca893441e2dbd7a00c10de1fb872865ccdf"]}
{"id": "clm:9cfd1dcb9879e1d33bd814efdffc1420d1d71e831ce7e912569ddfdbe04dbfb1", "type": "statement", "text": "Compass sampling documentation describes a 1,000-document $sample aggregation over a collection or query-selected subset. Treating such a sample as proof that no rare schema defect exists is an inference the evidence does not support. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/compass/sampling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e5b0820416bf1a9b86e1df0047ca695db12fa0a4e420c7b1c018b52de7ea93eb"]}
{"id": "clm:f1d3e702b84c88e93c3c327da9eb2b2253887ae0d457caad9eb24c89569117f9", "type": "statement", "text": "A schema-flexible database does not make inconsistent representations free. OneUptime recommends inspecting mixed field types, and independent document-database research explains that switching a logical value between scalar and array forms or mixing numeric and string representations complicates queries. This is design guidance, not evidence that Compass automatically flags every instance. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-compass-schema-analysis/view", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol18/p4804-carey.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:10bc55b5effd89063bee15f63980ad56205cd849bcac5158a705ce15fa8551e1", "ev:bd491af56039671f593181b89c6782f15a80d9f7f50cab11f17b3515cad78d14"]}
{"id": "clm:9d6a7e853f62c3c5497b71ea83eb9ede5cc8adb103f171810dd163ee2f403674", "type": "statement", "text": "Using data values such as dates as field names can make range queries awkward and prevent straightforward secondary indexing. The document-database design paper recommends explicit fields for those values; this is an additional manual review check, not a documented Compass detector. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol18/p4804-carey.pdf", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Compass Anti-Patterns"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e5fdbb7dd2ab4df031598b8335943c074d34a49ea056cd48d4701f1cb51420ca", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:9e2b141c528b9e59405f6444151e3b673ec3b5a860305f4f1f012b4b7677f10b"]}
